WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.983
Welcome to session 12 of the Lam Rim.

00:00:03.983 --> 00:00:06.283
And we've been talking about

00:00:06.283 --> 00:00:08.791
the place that compassion has

00:00:08.791 --> 00:00:11.122
in the five steps for getting to this

00:00:11.122 --> 00:00:14.347
bodhisattva vision: bodhichitta.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:18.325
And we reached the fifth
step, which is compassion.

00:00:18.325 --> 00:00:21.578
And we kind of are pausing
here to see how compassion

00:00:21.578 --> 00:00:25.568
is like the center of the propellor.

00:00:25.568 --> 00:00:30.172
All the other steps of the seven steps,

00:00:30.172 --> 00:00:32.982
they revolve around compassion.

00:00:32.982 --> 00:00:37.038
Somehow, compassion is at the root of

00:00:37.038 --> 00:00:38.880
beautiful love,

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.210
and at the root of recognizing the people

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:43.860
have been my mom, thinking
about what they did,

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.110
thinking to repay them.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:49.690
Somehow, compassion is at the center

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:52.233
of all these seven steps for getting to

00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:57.186
bodhichitta in the system
of Atisha, Lord Atisha.

00:00:57.186 --> 00:01:00.520
So we're going to continue on that theme.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.714
And ere at the beginning,

00:01:02.714 --> 00:01:06.550
we're going to get a quotation

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:08.591
from Master Chandrakirti.

00:01:08.591 --> 00:01:10.740
So Pabongka Rinpoche,

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.073
he's going to pull out a quotation
from Master Chandrakirti.

00:01:15.073 --> 00:01:19.846
I've been working on a
great, great commentary

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.770
by Je Tsongkapa

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:24.900
on this book by Chandrakirti,

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.490
called "Entering the Middle Way."

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.020
And Tsongkapa's book is
called DGONGS PA RAB GSAL

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:33.958
which means clarifying or
illuminating the true thought

00:01:33.958 --> 00:01:35.501
of Chandrakirti.

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:38.840
So, to get into this topic,

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.650
let's talk about about a special vision

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:42.522
that Je Tsongkapa had.

00:01:42.522 --> 00:01:45.013
Here's a picture of it.

00:01:45.013 --> 00:01:48.900
I wrote a long

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.440
history of Tsongkapa,
it took me many years.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.310
This particular scene

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:57.262
is 1397.

00:01:57.262 --> 00:02:00.870
You can see Je Tsongkapa
sitting at the bottom

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.565
in the yellow robe.

00:02:03.565 --> 00:02:06.380
And he's having a vision.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:10.250
I think, if my dating is
correct, it's the autumn

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.440
of 1397.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:16.110
Je Tsongkapa goes into this awesome vision

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.880
where he sees all the great teachers

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:21.200
of emptiness in history,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.810
the major teachers.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:27.428
You can see here, Nagarjuna at the top,

00:02:27.428 --> 00:02:31.700
and then we're going to have Buddhapalita

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:35.126
who wrote commentaries on Nagarjuna.

00:02:35.126 --> 00:02:38.620
Then we're going to have
probably Bhavaviveka,

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:42.560
who complained about
Buddhapalita's commentary.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.615
And then Chandrakirti,

00:02:44.615 --> 00:02:47.290
who complained to
Bhavaviveka for complaining

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:49.520
about Buddhapalita's commentary.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:53.360
So anyway, you're going to
have all the great teachers

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.740
of the emptiness lineage
here in this vision.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:59.390
There's a tradition that says that

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:02.908
this is when Je Tsongkapa
saw emptiness directly.

00:03:02.908 --> 00:03:06.320
So people often ask me,

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:10.001
was Je Tsongkapa an arya? And there is,

00:03:10.001 --> 00:03:14.976
the only mention of the
question is in this scene,

00:03:14.976 --> 00:03:17.650
in commentaries to this part of his life,

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:20.855
this moment in his life
that in conjunction with,

00:03:20.855 --> 00:03:25.210
apparently he saw the Buddhapalita
written across the sky

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.610
or something.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:30.650
And then they say that during that period,

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.125
he had the direct perception of emptiness.

00:03:33.125 --> 00:03:34.953
So that's our tradition.

00:03:34.953 --> 00:03:36.907
So I thought

00:03:36.907 --> 00:03:41.617
since Pabongka Rinpoche
is going to explain

00:03:41.617 --> 00:03:45.010
the role of compassion by going to

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:48.180
Chandrakirti's great book,
Entering the Middle Way,

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:50.315
why don't we go to

00:03:50.315 --> 00:03:53.830
Je Tsongkapa's commentary on this verse,

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.780
because I've been working
on that commentary

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:58.900
about seven years and it's very cool.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.378
So here we go.

00:04:00.378 --> 00:04:02.580
DPAL LDAN ZLA BAS KYANG

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:04.906
The glorious Chandrakirti,

00:04:04.906 --> 00:04:07.080
'JUG PA BRTZAMS PA'I THOG MAR

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:11.308
when he first started to
write his great classic

00:04:11.308 --> 00:04:16.306
Madhyamaka Avatara,
Entering the Middle Way.

00:04:16.306 --> 00:04:18.737
And by the way, Middle Way in that case

00:04:18.737 --> 00:04:21.290
doesn't mean philosophical Middle Way,

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:24.805
it means Nagarjuna's
root text called Wisdom.

00:04:24.805 --> 00:04:27.221
So Chandrakirti says

00:04:27.221 --> 00:04:29.713
,GANG PHYIR BRTZE NYID RGYAL
BA'I LO TOG PHUN TSOGS 'DI'I,

00:04:29.713 --> 00:04:32.821
,SA BON DANG NI SPEL LA
CHU 'DRA YUN RING DU,

00:04:32.821 --> 00:04:35.904
,LONGS SPYOD GNAS LA SMIN
PA LTA BUR 'DOD GYUR PA,

00:04:35.904 --> 00:04:38.520
,DE PHYIR BDAG GIS THOG MAR
SNYING RJER BSTOD PAR BGYI,

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.753
At the beginning

00:04:40.753 --> 00:04:43.960
of his greatest book,

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:46.990
one of the greatest books
ever written on emptiness,

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:49.180
Chandrakirti, Master Chandrakirti,

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.270
does not bow down to emptiness,

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:55.080
and he does not bow down to wisdom,

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.270
and he does not bow down to bodhichitta.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:00.713
He bows down to compassion.

00:05:00.713 --> 00:05:03.460
And he says, there's a reason.

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:08.290
So it fits into the Lam Rim so sweetly

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:12.120
that the Lam Rim guy stole
that verse for Lam Rim.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.610
So Chandrakirti says,

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:17.010
you want to understand emptiness?

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:18.940
Then get compassion.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:20.970
Then everybody's like, "What?

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:23.535
I thought I was supposed to meditate on

00:05:23.535 --> 00:05:24.398
shamata, vipashyana."

00:05:24.398 --> 00:05:27.233
- No, get compassion.

00:05:27.233 --> 00:05:30.654
Why and how? We're going
to go through it today.

00:05:30.654 --> 00:05:32.289
That's what our goal is.

00:05:32.289 --> 00:05:33.923
GANG PHYIR means because.

00:05:33.923 --> 00:05:38.923
BRTZE NYID love and
love alone is the seed,

00:05:38.935 --> 00:05:41.409
SA BON, in the second line.

00:05:41.409 --> 00:05:43.962
For RGYAL BA'I LO TOG PHUN TSOGS 'DI'I,

00:05:43.962 --> 00:05:48.930
for these luscious, generous
crops of the Buddhas.

00:05:51.044 --> 00:05:53.672
And t's like the seed

00:05:53.672 --> 00:05:57.112
for planting the crops of enlightenment.

00:05:57.112 --> 00:05:59.582
But it's also like the water that you add.

00:05:59.582 --> 00:06:02.380
So we had yesterday THOG MTHA' BAR GSUM.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:04.358
I'm sure you guys remember.

00:06:04.358 --> 00:06:06.365
THOG MTHA' BAR GSUM

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:09.173
Beginning, ending and in between.

00:06:09.173 --> 00:06:13.360
So Chandrakirti is saying, "Look,

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:16.165
why is compassion the
center of the seven?"

00:06:16.165 --> 00:06:21.150
Why did Tsongkapa present compassion

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:24.880
as the center of the seven
steps to bodhichitta?

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:29.570
Why did he present it as the central theme

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:34.300
or the middle of the whole machine?

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:37.188
He says, "Well, there's three reasons,

00:06:37.188 --> 00:06:39.464
THOG MTHA' BAR.

00:06:39.464 --> 00:06:42.170
In the beginning, you need compassion.

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:44.397
In the middle, you need compassion.

00:06:44.397 --> 00:06:46.820
And at the end, you need compassion.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:49.550
In his opening lines

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.240
of his famous book on emptiness,

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:55.900
Chandrakirti says, "It's like the seed,

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:57.580
it's like the water,

00:06:57.580 --> 00:06:59.578
and it's like the fruit."

00:06:59.578 --> 00:07:01.000
It's like the seed.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:02.720
It's like the water.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:04.400
And it's like the fruit.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:07.690
The seed of the fruit tree that you plant

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.450
is like the water that
you pour on the tree

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.210
before it grows fruit.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:14.440
Then it's like the
fruit that you can enjoy

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:17.533
once the tree grows and produces fruit.

00:07:17.533 --> 00:07:21.662
So compassion has a place THOG MTHA' BAR

00:07:21.662 --> 00:07:25.240
in the beginning of all
this process, like the seed;

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:27.135
in the middle of the process,

00:07:27.135 --> 00:07:29.563
like watering your garden every day;

00:07:29.563 --> 00:07:31.702
and then at the end of the process

00:07:31.702 --> 00:07:35.526
like eating the fruits that
grow out of your garden.

00:07:35.526 --> 00:07:37.500
Then Chandrakirti says,

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:41.030
"That's why I'm not bowing down to wisdom.

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:43.330
I'm not bowing down to emptiness.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:45.112
At the beginning of my book,

00:07:45.112 --> 00:07:47.344
I'm bowing down to compassion

00:07:47.344 --> 00:07:50.010
because it's the seed, it's the water

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:51.544
and it's the fruit."

00:07:51.544 --> 00:07:53.785
CHU 'DRA YUN RING DU, LONGS SPYOD GNAS LA

00:07:53.785 --> 00:07:55.451
LONGS SPYOD GNAS LA means

00:07:55.451 --> 00:07:58.510
and you're going to
enjoy it eating it later.

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:00.490
SMIN PA LTA BUR 'DOD GYUR PA

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:02.673
It's like the maturation of the fruit.

00:08:02.673 --> 00:08:05.264
DE PHYIR -- for that reason,

00:08:05.264 --> 00:08:09.501
BDAG GIS THOG MAR SNYING
RJE BSTOD PAR BGYI

00:08:09.501 --> 00:08:13.118
I'm going to bow down to compassion.

00:08:13.118 --> 00:08:16.342
All right, now I thought it would be fun,

00:08:16.342 --> 00:08:20.780
since this Lam Rim is going so fast,

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:23.327
if we added some more stuff.

00:08:23.327 --> 00:08:27.432
So let's go look at what
Tsongkapa has to say

00:08:27.432 --> 00:08:29.813
about this verse by Chandrakirti.

00:08:29.813 --> 00:08:32.580
Let's go look at Tsongkapa's explanation.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:35.422
And again, I added this part.

00:08:35.422 --> 00:08:38.007
This is DGONGS PA RAB GSAL.

00:08:38.007 --> 00:08:41.440
Je Tsongkapa's "Illumination
of the True Thought".

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:43.176
And let's read it together.

00:08:43.176 --> 00:08:45.660
Because this Lam Rim's going too fast.

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:48.190
We're going to finish in 15-20 years.

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:52.100
Let's slow it down a little bit.

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:55.778
GNYIS PA NI, BYANG CHUB KYI
SEMS DANG GNYIS SU MED PA'I

00:08:55.778 --> 00:08:59.417
YE SHES GNYIS KYI RTZA BA
YANG SNYING RJE YIN PAS NA,

00:08:59.417 --> 00:09:02.617
Look, there's two important
spiritual goals we have

00:09:02.617 --> 00:09:06.780
with this book by Chandrakirti,
by Master Chandrakirti.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:08.180
What are they?

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.893
BYANG CHUB KYI SEMS

00:09:09.893 --> 00:09:12.382
We want to get to that bodhisattva vision.

00:09:12.382 --> 00:09:14.980
We want to get to the
Wish for enlightenment.

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:17.664
And we want the GNYIS SU MED PA'I YE SHES.

00:09:17.664 --> 00:09:22.555
We want the indivisible wisdom,

00:09:22.555 --> 00:09:26.770
the wisdom which is free of two things.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:31.020
The wisdom which is free of two things.

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:34.315
People call it non-duality
or something like that.

00:09:34.315 --> 00:09:39.300
I feel a little
uncomfortable with the word.

00:09:43.083 --> 00:09:46.264
People think it means
when you see emptiness.

00:09:46.264 --> 00:09:49.703
There's no me and there's no emptiness.

00:09:49.703 --> 00:09:51.660
No duality.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:54.483
I sink into the emptiness,
there's no perceiver

00:09:54.483 --> 00:09:56.318
and there's no perceived.

00:09:56.318 --> 00:09:58.900
And people say, "Oh, that's non-duality."

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:00.520
That's not non-duality.

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:04.000
Non-duality means discrepancy.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:05.500
Discrepancy.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.350
What's discrepancy mean?

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:08.880
It means

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:12.100
there's a difference between
the way this guy acts

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:13.970
and the way he really is.

00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:16.261
There's a discrepancy.

00:10:16.261 --> 00:10:18.923
He says he's

00:10:18.923 --> 00:10:22.698
a Lam Rim teacher and he never meditates.

00:10:22.698 --> 00:10:24.702
That's a discrepancy.

00:10:24.702 --> 00:10:26.610
That's a discrepancy.

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:28.580
So discrepancy means

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:31.840
it looks like one way and
it's really a different way.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:34.975
And that's what duality means in Buddhism.

00:10:34.975 --> 00:10:37.070
It means discrepancy.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.655
It means they don't match.

00:10:39.655 --> 00:10:41.990
The way things are

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:43.900
and the way things look

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:45.260
don't match.

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:49.430
It looks like your husband
is upset in the kitchen

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:52.868
because he had a hard day at his job.

00:10:52.868 --> 00:10:56.288
But what's really happening is you

00:10:56.288 --> 00:10:58.670
yelled at your kids last night.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:00.470
So they don't fit.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:02.370
There's a discrepancy

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.290
between the way it looks

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:05.440
and the way it is.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:08.430
When you catch the discrepancy,

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.693
when you realize

00:11:10.693 --> 00:11:14.775
how hard was his job today has
nothing to do with his mood.

00:11:14.775 --> 00:11:18.467
His mood is coming from how you
treated your kids last week.

00:11:18.467 --> 00:11:22.510
Then you free yourself of this duality.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:23.470
That's all.

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:25.180
The way it looks

00:11:25.180 --> 00:11:26.905
and the way it really is

00:11:26.905 --> 00:11:28.740
don't match.

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:30.578
That's called non-duality.

00:11:30.578 --> 00:11:32.008
When you figure it out,

00:11:32.008 --> 00:11:35.867
we call it non-dual wisdom.

00:11:35.867 --> 00:11:39.260
It doesn't see two
different things anymore.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:40.580
It sees one thing.

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:42.270
I yelled at my kids.

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:44.503
It doesn't see a husband who's upset

00:11:44.503 --> 00:11:47.113
because he's hungry or
something like that.

00:11:47.113 --> 00:11:50.483
Although husbands do get upset
when they're hungry, right?

00:11:50.483 --> 00:11:53.567
At least this husband does.

00:11:53.567 --> 00:11:57.550
So don't forget, when I say non-duality,

00:11:57.550 --> 00:12:01.085
it means the way he looks

00:12:01.085 --> 00:12:02.597
and he way he really is

00:12:02.597 --> 00:12:04.226
are going to match now.

00:12:04.226 --> 00:12:05.226
Non-duality.

00:12:05.226 --> 00:12:07.092
Now they're going to match.

00:12:07.092 --> 00:12:09.918
Oh, he's upset cause I
yelled at my kids last week.

00:12:09.918 --> 00:12:11.818
Oh, now it matches up.

00:12:11.818 --> 00:12:16.718
So he says two great
spiritual goals here are:

00:12:16.718 --> 00:12:20.200
bodhichitta, the wish to become
a Buddha to help all beings,

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:23.111
dance between planets;

00:12:23.111 --> 00:12:26.659
and this wisdom which no longer separates,

00:12:26.659 --> 00:12:28.401
now this wisdom sees

00:12:28.401 --> 00:12:30.909
what's really going on.

00:12:30.909 --> 00:12:34.322
Then he says a interesting thing.

00:12:34.322 --> 00:12:36.683
This is Chandrakirti.

00:12:36.683 --> 00:12:40.540
This is the root of all
emptiness books in Tibet,

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:41.867
Chandrakirti.

00:12:41.867 --> 00:12:46.862
And he says, the root of
those two is compassion.

00:12:48.795 --> 00:12:51.312
Then we're like, "What?"

00:12:51.312 --> 00:12:53.628
Okay, I understand the bodhichitta,

00:12:53.628 --> 00:12:55.596
I understand that compassion

00:12:55.596 --> 00:12:58.280
can be the root of
bodhichitta, I understand that.

00:12:58.280 --> 00:12:59.664
That makes sense.

00:12:59.664 --> 00:13:01.455
You got to have compassion,

00:13:01.455 --> 00:13:04.041
step number five of the seven steps,

00:13:04.041 --> 00:13:08.034
to get to this vision of a Bodhisattva.

00:13:08.034 --> 00:13:11.092
Why does compassion lead
you to understand your

00:13:11.092 --> 00:13:13.050
husband in the kitchen?

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:15.066
Now that part I don't get.

00:13:15.066 --> 00:13:17.375
But Chandrakirti is insistent.

00:13:17.375 --> 00:13:22.320
In the beginning lines of
my book about emptiness,

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:24.578
I'm not going to talk about emptiness.

00:13:24.578 --> 00:13:27.299
I'm going to talk about
the cause of emptiness

00:13:27.299 --> 00:13:29.278
because that's more important.

00:13:29.278 --> 00:13:32.095
What's the cause? Compassion. What?

00:13:32.095 --> 00:13:34.462
Well, can't a lower arhat see emptiness?

00:13:34.462 --> 00:13:36.330
It gets confusing, right?

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:39.820
So we're going to explore
that in this class.

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:42.200
We're going to explore that in this class.

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:44.950
And I'm not going to tell you an answer.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:47.310
I want you to think about it.

00:13:47.310 --> 00:13:49.284
I want you guys to figure it out.

00:13:49.284 --> 00:13:54.172
That's your homework for
the next 10 years or so.

00:13:54.172 --> 00:13:59.158
Chandrakirti refuses
to bow down to wisdom.

00:13:59.158 --> 00:14:03.593
He refuses to bow down to
the perception of emptiness.

00:14:03.593 --> 00:14:04.890
He says, "No,

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:07.660
compassion is the cause of that

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:09.292
seeing emptiness directly.

00:14:09.292 --> 00:14:11.007
So let's bow down to that."

00:14:11.007 --> 00:14:14.763
And by the way, it's also
the cause of bodhisattva.

00:14:14.763 --> 00:14:19.592
And by the way, he takes it one more step.

00:14:19.592 --> 00:14:23.457
Compassion causes bodhichitta

00:14:23.457 --> 00:14:25.580
and the perception of emptiness,

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:27.912
and they create arhats and Buddhas.

00:14:27.912 --> 00:14:30.160
So he goes like that.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:35.160
Compassion causes emptiness
understanding and bodhichitta,

00:14:35.963 --> 00:14:40.082
and they create Buddhas and arhats.

00:14:40.082 --> 00:14:42.690
Like that. He has a flow like that.

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:45.160
Now I'm going to read you Tsongkapa,

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.018
and you're going to figure out,

00:14:47.018 --> 00:14:51.993
why does he bow down to compassion

00:14:51.993 --> 00:14:54.700
and says it creates wisdom?

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:55.870
That's confusing.

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:59.661
DE GSUM GYI NANG NAS
SNYING RJE GTZO BO NYID DU

00:14:59.661 --> 00:15:02.155
BSTAN PAR BZHED NAS,

00:15:02.155 --> 00:15:04.870
Chandrakirti wants to say

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:09.850
that of bodhichitta, and the
direct perception of emptiness,

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:12.360
and compassion,

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:14.482
compassion is the most important.

00:15:14.482 --> 00:15:17.008
That's the root.

00:15:17.008 --> 00:15:18.760
GTZO BO NYID means like,

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:20.915
we have it in LAM GTZO RNAM GSUM,

00:15:20.915 --> 00:15:22.362
Three Principle Paths.

00:15:22.362 --> 00:15:25.123
The main one is compassion.

00:15:25.123 --> 00:15:28.324
BZHED NAS, GANG PHYIR ZHES SOGS GSUNGS SO,

00:15:28.324 --> 00:15:30.219
That's why he wrote this verse.

00:15:30.219 --> 00:15:33.300
We can see a picture here of a tree

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:37.030
with a bunch of big roots.

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:41.240
And I was trying to find a thing,

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:44.000
it's like the one root
which leads to the two roots

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.508
which leads to the tree.

00:15:45.508 --> 00:15:47.300
The tree is Buddhahood

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:49.660
and nirvana.

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:53.000
The two roots are

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:55.720
perceiving emptiness and bodhichitta.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.355
And the root of those

00:15:57.355 --> 00:15:58.813
is compassion.

00:15:58.813 --> 00:15:59.646
Great.

00:15:59.646 --> 00:16:02.463
So I've tried to find a
picture for that, good luck.

00:16:02.463 --> 00:16:04.233
This is the closest I can find.

00:16:04.233 --> 00:16:05.852
All right.

00:16:05.852 --> 00:16:09.647
Now let's go back to the text.

00:16:10.856 --> 00:16:13.920
Then Tsongkapa uses the
verse, he quotes the verse.

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:18.820
Now I'm going to skip to GANG GI PHYIR.

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:22.411
GANG GI PHYIR SNYING BRTZE
BA NI RGYAL BA'I LO TOG

00:16:22.411 --> 00:16:23.762
PHUN TSOGS 'DI'I

00:16:23.762 --> 00:16:25.795
You can think of

00:16:25.795 --> 00:16:28.543
Buddhas as the crops.

00:16:28.543 --> 00:16:33.505
You can think of Buddha as the fruit tree.

00:16:33.505 --> 00:16:35.970
Pachi, what were the main
trees you guys planted in

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:37.690
Costa Rica?

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:41.523
Any fruit trees? Coffee trees? No.

00:16:41.523 --> 00:16:43.360
Mix of everything.

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:47.385
Let's do coffee tree
cause I'm in the mood.

00:16:47.385 --> 00:16:51.635
Coffee tree or coffee bush
really? Bush, I guess.

00:16:51.635 --> 00:16:55.020
So Buddhahood is the coffee bush.

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:57.852
I guess.

00:16:57.852 --> 00:16:59.310
Doesn't quite fit.

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:01.370
It's more like crops.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:04.134
Let's say corn.

00:17:04.134 --> 00:17:08.388
THOG MAR SKYED PA LA GAL
CHE BA SA BON DANG NI 'DRA

00:17:08.388 --> 00:17:11.030
The first thing you need
for a tree is a seed.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:13.289
Therefore, you need compassion.

00:17:13.289 --> 00:17:14.931
BAR DU, in the middle,

00:17:14.931 --> 00:17:18.097
GONG NAS GONG DU SPEL BA LA CHU DANG 'DRA

00:17:18.097 --> 00:17:20.640
In between, compassion is important

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:22.173
because it's like the water

00:17:22.173 --> 00:17:25.105
that you put on the seed.

00:17:25.105 --> 00:17:28.978
THA MAR GDUL BYAS YUN RING
DU LONGS SPYOD PA'I GNAS LA

00:17:28.978 --> 00:17:31.538
And in the end, after
the fruit tree grows,

00:17:31.538 --> 00:17:36.518
people can eat those mangoes forever.

00:17:36.518 --> 00:17:38.208
Buddhahood GNAS LA.

00:17:38.208 --> 00:17:40.858
'BRAS BU'I SMIN PA LTA BUR
'DOD PAR GYUR PA DE'I PHYIR,

00:17:40.858 --> 00:17:45.832
ZLA BA'I ZHABS BDAG GIS NYAN
RANG DANG SANGS RGYAS DANG,

00:17:45.832 --> 00:17:47.652
BYANG SEMS DANG DE'I RGYU
GZHAN GNYIS LAS KYANG

00:17:47.652 --> 00:17:49.609
THOG MAR RAM, BSTAN
BCOS RTZOM BA'I THOG MAR

00:17:49.609 --> 00:17:52.176
SNYING RJE CHEN PO LA BSTOD PAR BGYI'O

00:17:52.176 --> 00:17:54.565
I'm going to, Chandrakirti is saying

00:17:54.565 --> 00:17:58.082
I'm bowing down at the
beginning of my book

00:17:58.082 --> 00:18:00.660
not to the perception of emptiness

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:02.620
and not to bodhichitta,

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:05.110
but to the cause for both of those,

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:08.110
which is compassion.

00:18:09.677 --> 00:18:13.050
Because this is the
opening verse of that book,

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:18.050
which is the mother book of
all emptiness books in Tibetan.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:20.681
Let's go to the next line, next paragraph.

00:18:20.681 --> 00:18:24.064
DE YANG DA GZOD BSTOD
PA MIN GYI DE MA THAG TU

00:18:24.064 --> 00:18:28.256
RGYAL BA'I LO TOG BSKRUN PA LA,

00:18:28.256 --> 00:18:32.064
THOG MTHA' BAR GSUM DU GAL
CHE BAR BSTAN PA DE NYID DE,

00:18:32.064 --> 00:18:35.165
NYID KYI SGRAS NI DPE'I
SKABS SU PHYI'I LO TOG LA

00:18:35.165 --> 00:18:36.813
THOG MTHA' BAR GSUM

00:18:36.813 --> 00:18:40.133
The point of this next paragraph

00:18:40.133 --> 00:18:45.051
is that Chandrakirti says,

00:18:45.051 --> 00:18:47.409
"Love and only love is the main root."

00:18:47.409 --> 00:18:50.867
Love and only love is the main root.

00:18:50.867 --> 00:18:53.752
And when he means is, yes

00:18:53.752 --> 00:18:55.690
I'm comparing love

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:59.000
to three stages in the
growth of a fruit tree.

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:01.000
I'm comparing love

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:02.880
to three stages

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:04.880
in the growth of a fruit tree.

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:08.590
But please remember, I'm
talking about the same love.

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:10.450
The seed is the love.

00:19:10.450 --> 00:19:12.360
The water is the love.

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:14.229
The fruit of the tree is the love.

00:19:14.229 --> 00:19:16.400
All three are love.

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:18.780
Sorry, compassion.

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:21.263
All right.

00:19:21.263 --> 00:19:24.352
I'm going to start the next paragraph.

00:19:24.352 --> 00:19:27.619
Oh, you have a picture here

00:19:29.352 --> 00:19:32.718
of a tree and some fruits,

00:19:32.718 --> 00:19:35.380
or some flowers on the tree.

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:39.160
Yeah, I took this picture
at my house a few days ago,

00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:41.920
and I planted a peach tree.

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:44.397
I planted two peach
trees at the Black Hole,

00:19:44.397 --> 00:19:48.288
I mean, the Peach Tree Cafe.

00:19:48.288 --> 00:19:50.682
Then I had an extra one, so I took it home

00:19:50.682 --> 00:19:54.988
and I planted it there.

00:19:54.988 --> 00:19:59.742
It just grew very well and
this is the first year.

00:19:59.742 --> 00:20:02.070
Usually you don't get
fruit the first year.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:04.477
But it flowered, the whole tree flowered

00:20:04.477 --> 00:20:05.785
the first year.

00:20:05.785 --> 00:20:07.975
So it's a baby, baby, baby tree.

00:20:07.975 --> 00:20:10.910
But these are the flowers.

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:14.540
So, when you look at that picture,

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:17.570
you can think about the
flowers are like the

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:20.216
fruit of the tree.

00:20:20.216 --> 00:20:22.775
The tree is the... and
then there's the water

00:20:22.775 --> 00:20:26.961
that I put on the tree all winter.

00:20:26.961 --> 00:20:30.252
And then there's the seed,

00:20:30.252 --> 00:20:33.860
the peach pit, from
which we grew the tree.

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:37.539
All right, we're going to
start now, Pau, with THOG MAR.

00:20:37.539 --> 00:20:40.486
It's the paragraph that
begins with THOG MAR.

00:20:40.486 --> 00:20:42.419
THOG MAR GAL CHE BA LA

00:20:42.419 --> 00:20:46.486
THOG MAR GAL CHE BA LA
SA BON LTA BU YIN TSUL

00:20:46.486 --> 00:20:48.640
What's important at the beginning

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:50.440
is you've got to have a seed.

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:54.033
'DI LTAR SNYING RJE CHEN PO
CAN NI SEMS CAN GYI SDUG BSGNAL

00:20:54.033 --> 00:20:58.008
GYIS SDUG BSNGAL BAS, SDUG
BSNGAL CAN GYI SEMS CAN THAMS CAD

00:20:58.008 --> 00:21:00.198
BSKYAB PA'I PHYIR DU

00:21:00.198 --> 00:21:02.668
If you want to take care
of all living beings

00:21:02.668 --> 00:21:04.701
who are suffering like your mom

00:21:04.701 --> 00:21:08.490
who's blind and went crazy and
is about to fall off a cliff,

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:11.222
BDAG GIS SEMS CAN 'DI THAMS CAD 'KHOR BA'I

00:21:11.222 --> 00:21:13.322
SDUG BSNGAL NAS BTON TE

00:21:13.322 --> 00:21:15.723
I'm going to get all
of these living beings

00:21:15.723 --> 00:21:16.768
out of sansara.

00:21:16.768 --> 00:21:19.724
SANGS RGYAS LA NGES PAR SBYAR BAR BYA'O

00:21:19.724 --> 00:21:22.183
I will get them to enlightenment.

00:21:22.183 --> 00:21:24.860
BYA BA LA DMIGS PA'I SEMS BSKYED LA

00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:27.455
So isn't that the essence of bodhichitta?

00:21:27.455 --> 00:21:32.146
So that's easy. You have to

00:21:32.146 --> 00:21:35.020
want to get people out of pain

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:38.480
if you want to reach Buddhahood
to help all living beings.

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:41.305
First, you have to want to
get them out of trouble.

00:21:41.305 --> 00:21:43.127
Then you can have bodhichitta.

00:21:43.127 --> 00:21:45.479
So first, you've got to have compassion

00:21:45.479 --> 00:21:47.573
and then you can have bodhichitta.

00:21:47.573 --> 00:21:48.723
And I would say,

00:21:48.723 --> 00:21:50.985
first, you have to feel their pain

00:21:50.985 --> 00:21:53.850
before you can want to get
them out of their pain.

00:21:53.850 --> 00:21:56.120
First, you have to feel...

00:21:56.120 --> 00:22:00.088
First you have to feel what
the other person is feeling

00:22:00.088 --> 00:22:02.681
before you want to save them.

00:22:02.681 --> 00:22:06.040
So bodhichitta is like
you want to save them.

00:22:06.040 --> 00:22:07.950
But first you have to
feel what they're feeling.

00:22:07.950 --> 00:22:11.167
Otherwise, you won't want to save them.

00:22:11.167 --> 00:22:14.320
You have to imagine what it's like to be

00:22:14.320 --> 00:22:18.385
crazy, and blind, and
up on a mountain cliff

00:22:18.385 --> 00:22:20.920
before you can try to help your mom.

00:22:20.920 --> 00:22:23.130
You have to imagine how she feels,

00:22:23.130 --> 00:22:26.036
how it feels to be your mom.

00:22:26.036 --> 00:22:27.447
All right.

00:22:27.447 --> 00:22:28.888
But we're waiting for,

00:22:28.888 --> 00:22:31.387
I don't know about you,
Pau and Pachi, Cristina,

00:22:31.387 --> 00:22:33.328
I'm waiting to see

00:22:33.328 --> 00:22:37.212
how's he going to connect
it to seeing emptiness?

00:22:37.212 --> 00:22:40.730
I can understand the bodhichitta part.

00:22:40.730 --> 00:22:42.258
Let's keep going.

00:22:42.258 --> 00:22:44.866
DE YANG RANG GIS SANGS RGYAS THOB PA LA

00:22:44.866 --> 00:22:47.048
RAG LAS PAR MTHONG NAS

00:22:47.048 --> 00:22:49.217
Well, if I really want to help my mom,

00:22:49.217 --> 00:22:51.668
I have to have the power to help my mom.

00:22:51.668 --> 00:22:54.400
And for that, I need to become a Buddha.

00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:57.865
BDAG GIS 'DI RNAMS KYI DON
DU BLA MED BYANG CHUB CI NAS

00:22:57.865 --> 00:22:59.265
KYANG THOB PAR BYA'O

00:22:59.265 --> 00:23:01.450
So I'm going to have to become a Buddha.

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:03.329
Okay, that's clear.

00:23:03.329 --> 00:23:06.230
BYANG CHUB LA DMIGS PA'I
SEMS NGES PAR BSKYED DO

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:09.210
So don't forget, sometimes bodhichitta

00:23:09.210 --> 00:23:11.580
is called the state of
mind with two focuses.

00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:13.320
What are they?

00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:15.943
I'm focused on

00:23:15.943 --> 00:23:19.042
others and I want to achieve

00:23:19.042 --> 00:23:22.340
Buddhahood. So it's called
the mind with two focuses.

00:23:22.340 --> 00:23:25.290
Sometimes bodhichitta is called
the mind with two focuses.

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:28.430
Now, as far as this part
about achieving Buddhahood,

00:23:28.430 --> 00:23:30.980
okay, I want to help everybody

00:23:30.980 --> 00:23:33.670
so I'm going to have
to achieve Buddhahood.

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:36.885
Next paragraph.

00:23:38.580 --> 00:23:41.520
I have this picture I found, I don't know,

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:46.511
it's kind of pushing it, right?

00:23:48.253 --> 00:23:50.828
In DCI, we call it...

00:23:50.828 --> 00:23:52.540
What do you call that?

00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:57.481
Reverse engineering?

00:23:57.481 --> 00:24:00.303
I used to go to Switzerland

00:24:00.303 --> 00:24:03.040
for jewelry shows.

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:07.586
And there'll be 10,000
people there showing jewelry.

00:24:07.586 --> 00:24:12.549
Unbelievable. Basel,
Switzerland. Every year.

00:24:12.549 --> 00:24:17.485
People will go there to buy jewelry,

00:24:17.485 --> 00:24:21.500
but manufacturers will go there to buy

00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:24.583
other company's jewelry and steal it.

00:24:25.600 --> 00:24:27.548
So you see,

00:24:27.548 --> 00:24:31.230
you go to the trade show,

00:24:31.230 --> 00:24:34.620
the audiences are massing
in front of one new product,

00:24:34.620 --> 00:24:36.780
and you go and buy one.

00:24:36.780 --> 00:24:38.960
Even though it helps your competition,

00:24:38.960 --> 00:24:40.370
you buy one.

00:24:40.370 --> 00:24:43.450
Even if it's $10,000, you buy one.

00:24:43.450 --> 00:24:46.340
And you take it home
and you take it apart,

00:24:46.340 --> 00:24:48.610
and you figure out how did they make it.

00:24:48.610 --> 00:24:50.660
That's called reverse engineering.

00:24:50.660 --> 00:24:53.330
And it's very, very common in everything,

00:24:53.330 --> 00:24:55.330
every kind of product.

00:24:55.330 --> 00:24:59.330
You go buy the latest printer

00:24:59.330 --> 00:25:01.270
and then you take it
apart and you figure out

00:25:01.270 --> 00:25:02.780
how to copy it.

00:25:02.780 --> 00:25:05.560
So anyway, that's called
reverse engineering.

00:25:05.560 --> 00:25:09.045
So what I'm saying is,

00:25:09.045 --> 00:25:11.520
let's start with enlightenment

00:25:11.520 --> 00:25:14.040
and let's work backwards to bodhichitta

00:25:14.040 --> 00:25:16.060
and emptiness perception,

00:25:16.060 --> 00:25:21.060
and then we'll work
backwards to compassion.

00:25:21.390 --> 00:25:24.023
DE 'DRA BA'I DAM BCA' BA DE
YANG GNYIS SU MED PA'I YE SHES

00:25:24.023 --> 00:25:28.606
KYIS MTSON PA'I SBYIN SOGS KYI
SPYOD PA DOR NA MI 'GRUB PAR

00:25:28.606 --> 00:25:31.123
You can not...

00:25:31.123 --> 00:25:33.497
Now here's the emptiness one.

00:25:33.497 --> 00:25:36.980
$100 to whoever can tell it to me first.

00:25:36.980 --> 00:25:38.210
You ready?

00:25:38.210 --> 00:25:41.370
By the way, I'm not offering
it to everybody at home,

00:25:41.370 --> 00:25:44.500
I'm just offering it to the people here.

00:25:44.500 --> 00:25:45.333
$100.

00:25:47.750 --> 00:25:51.550
Here's the sentence where
Tsongkapa explains our question,

00:25:51.550 --> 00:25:53.940
but it's not obvious.

00:25:53.940 --> 00:25:55.380
DE 'DRA BA'I DAM BCA' BA DE

00:25:55.380 --> 00:25:57.030
Look, you made a promise, right?

00:25:57.030 --> 00:25:58.040
What?

00:25:58.040 --> 00:26:01.923
I'm going to achieve
enlightenment for all my moms.

00:26:01.923 --> 00:26:04.600
Well, for that, you're
going to have to practice

00:26:04.600 --> 00:26:07.040
the six perfections.

00:26:07.040 --> 00:26:11.223
Therefore, emptiness.

00:26:14.864 --> 00:26:16.570
Come on, $100.

00:26:16.570 --> 00:26:18.655
Come on. Just say something.

00:26:18.655 --> 00:26:21.200
[Student] Understand emptiness.

00:26:21.200 --> 00:26:22.840
[GMR] I'll say it again.

00:26:22.840 --> 00:26:25.248
Here's what he says.

00:26:25.248 --> 00:26:29.020
To fulfill the wish of bodhichitta,

00:26:29.020 --> 00:26:30.970
you're going to have to become a Buddha.

00:26:30.970 --> 00:26:32.621
To become a Buddha, you're
going to have to follow

00:26:32.621 --> 00:26:33.986
the six perfections.

00:26:33.986 --> 00:26:36.853
That's why I say emptiness is the root.

00:26:36.853 --> 00:26:40.827
[Student] (unclear)

00:26:44.456 --> 00:26:49.022
[GMR] Connected to the perfection.

00:26:49.022 --> 00:26:54.022
[Student] One feels what
another feels. [GMR] No.

00:26:54.030 --> 00:26:57.812
[Student] ...because you
see emptiness. [GMR] No.

00:26:57.812 --> 00:27:01.728
Okay, for $50.

00:27:01.728 --> 00:27:04.520
The sixth perfection is
said to be the result,

00:27:04.520 --> 00:27:05.470
sorry,

00:27:05.470 --> 00:27:07.200
the first five perfections

00:27:07.200 --> 00:27:10.170
are said to be the result
of the sixth perfection.

00:27:15.800 --> 00:27:18.510
Practicing giving, for example,

00:27:18.510 --> 00:27:23.370
is only a perfection if you do it with...

00:27:23.370 --> 00:27:24.911
[Student] emptiness.

00:27:24.911 --> 00:27:26.694
[GMR] Yay! So that's a 20 dollars answer.

00:27:26.694 --> 00:27:28.330
Okay, $20 answer.

00:27:28.330 --> 00:27:29.340
Isn't that cool?

00:27:29.340 --> 00:27:32.330
So he says, "Ah, the mystery is solved."

00:27:32.330 --> 00:27:34.478
- What mystery?

00:27:34.478 --> 00:27:37.770
- Supposedly compassion is
the root of seeing emptiness?

00:27:37.770 --> 00:27:39.090
- Yeah.

00:27:39.090 --> 00:27:40.100
- Why?

00:27:40.100 --> 00:27:41.910
- Compassion wants to become a Buddha.

00:27:41.910 --> 00:27:42.940
- Okay.

00:27:42.940 --> 00:27:45.960
- That means compassion wants
to practice the 6 perfections.

00:27:45.960 --> 00:27:46.860
- Okay.

00:27:46.860 --> 00:27:50.370
- But a perfection is not a
perfection unless you do it with

00:27:50.370 --> 00:27:51.600
emptiness perception.

00:27:51.600 --> 00:27:55.040
Therefore, compassion leads to

00:27:55.040 --> 00:27:56.340
emptiness perception.

00:27:56.340 --> 00:27:58.680
Because compassion leads to the intention

00:27:58.680 --> 00:28:00.450
of practicing emptiness,

00:28:00.450 --> 00:28:01.640
so you can become a Buddha.

00:28:01.640 --> 00:28:03.070
Got it?

00:28:03.070 --> 00:28:04.280
Yay!

00:28:04.280 --> 00:28:06.961
Okay, the mystery is solved.

00:28:07.895 --> 00:28:09.145
KHO NAR 'JUG PAS NA,

00:28:09.145 --> 00:28:13.690
We can skip the rest of that sentence.

00:28:13.690 --> 00:28:15.747
Let's go to the

00:28:15.747 --> 00:28:17.430
last line here.

00:28:17.430 --> 00:28:19.708
The last verse here.

00:28:19.708 --> 00:28:24.692
And he's going back to Arya Nagarjuna's

00:28:24.692 --> 00:28:27.634
String of Jewels, Ratnavali.

00:28:27.634 --> 00:28:31.170
vāli or valī, I don't know.

00:28:31.170 --> 00:28:35.075
We're going back to the
String of Precious Jewels by

00:28:35.075 --> 00:28:36.310
Arya Nagarjuna.

00:28:36.310 --> 00:28:38.603
And here's our final

00:28:38.603 --> 00:28:41.085
verse for our class.

00:28:41.085 --> 00:28:44.634
DON 'DI LA DGONGS NAS
RIN CHEN 'PHRENG BA LAS

00:28:44.634 --> 00:28:48.110
Arya Nagarjuna is talking
about the same idea

00:28:48.110 --> 00:28:50.890
in his String of Precious Jewels

00:28:50.890 --> 00:28:52.637
when he says,

00:28:52.637 --> 00:28:54.686
,THEG PA CHEN PO GANG ZHIG LAS,

00:28:54.686 --> 00:28:56.570
,SNYING RJE SNGON BTANG SPYOD KUN DANG,

00:28:56.570 --> 00:28:58.536
,YE SHES DRI MA MED BSHAD PA,

00:28:58.536 --> 00:29:01.178
,SEMS YOD SU ZHIG DE LA SMOD,

00:29:01.178 --> 00:29:03.280
He says,

00:29:03.280 --> 00:29:07.100
"you guys, if you have
any brains at all..."

00:29:07.100 --> 00:29:12.100
This is very Nagarjuna,
the last line. SEMS YOD

00:29:12.240 --> 00:29:15.228
SEMS YOD -- If you have any brains at all,

00:29:15.228 --> 00:29:17.150
you should study the Mahayana.

00:29:17.150 --> 00:29:20.858
You should go straight to
the compassion vehicle.

00:29:20.858 --> 00:29:23.770
And what's that one?

00:29:23.770 --> 00:29:27.860
Oh, it includes compassion

00:29:27.860 --> 00:29:29.740
and wisdom.

00:29:29.740 --> 00:29:32.322
It includes compassion and wisdom.

00:29:32.322 --> 00:29:36.160
Mahayana is just wisdom
married to compassion.

00:29:36.160 --> 00:29:37.851
That's all.

00:29:37.851 --> 00:29:39.580
THEG PA CHEN PO GANG ZHIG LAS

00:29:39.580 --> 00:29:42.520
And if you think that's a dumb idea,

00:29:42.520 --> 00:29:44.500
you ain't got any brains.

00:29:44.500 --> 00:29:47.016
SEMS YOD SU ZHIG DE LA SMOD means,

00:29:47.016 --> 00:29:49.491
if you think it's a dumb idea

00:29:49.491 --> 00:29:54.020
to combine wisdom with compassion,

00:29:54.020 --> 00:29:56.680
to reach Buddhahood and bodhichitta,

00:29:56.680 --> 00:30:00.777
then I'm afraid you don't
got any brains at all.

00:30:00.777 --> 00:30:02.610
All right, we finished the class.

00:30:02.610 --> 00:30:03.870
Good job you guys.

00:30:03.870 --> 00:30:05.390
Good job on the tech side

00:30:05.390 --> 00:30:07.130
and the Sanskrit side.

00:30:07.130 --> 00:30:08.490
Thank you.

00:30:08.490 --> 00:30:10.346
And we'll see you guys in the next class.

00:30:10.346 --> 00:30:11.179
Yay!

